ng happened and  of course where is brian laundry thank  you both coming up on law and crime  daily the medical examiner takes the  stand in the trial of a u.s airman mark  gooch plus a look inside the intimate  relationship of elizabeth holmes and  sonny bowani the latest in her federal  trial after the break  [Music]  welcome back personal text messages come  to light in the federal trial of  elizabeth holmes on tuesday jurors saw  the back and forth between holmes and  former romantic partner ramesh sunny  balwani  the texts show the pair collected  upwards of 250 million dollars from  investors including rupert murdoch just  days after a lab director quit due to  compliance issues but wani replied to  the text quote they are not investing in  our company they are investing in our  destiny former theron's lab director  adam rosendorf testifying he felt  theranose higher-ups would not provide  resources needed for proficiency tests  founded back in 2003 holmes claimed the  now-defunct theranos would revolutionize  blood testing later investigations found  many issues with its programs the former  billionaire faces 12 fraud charges in  connection to her time with the company  let's bring back legal analyst dina dahl  and co-host terry austin terry how  damning are these text messages and do  they rule out any argument that holmes  may have been forced to act based on her  relationship with bowani  those text messages are very damning and  very insightful they're showing that  there is fraud because they're  soliciting funds a lot of money frankly  and they know that there are problems  with their testing and when you have a  lab director get on the stand and say  that he was talking about quality  control issues and his warnings were  ignored that's a big problem so far also  brian i haven't seen any evidence that  bowani was the one who was controlling  this was a power couple but the power  behind this couple was definitely  elizabeth holmes now dean of the powers  behind elizabeth holmes belwani has to  be watching holmes trial do you think  what is coming out in the trial is  making bowani's future trial that much  harder for him  i actually think it makes it easier he  gets to see  what holes maybe he can poke you know  the defense attorney and also i imagine  we're going to see him blame elizabeth  holmes just like we're seeing her blame  him  whether or not the jury buys that or not  we'll see so  but i do think it could help him to see  in hindsight what worked and didn't work  for her yeah i think both sides are  going to end up doing the proverbial  throwing each other under the bus  the downside here is often times there's  space enough on that bus for two we'll  continue to follow this case and see how  it progresses thank you both in other  top legal news the trial for an army  veteran accused of breaking into  buildings and landmarks to take daring  photos is delayed so he can get a mental  health evaluation isaac wright traveled  the country scaling buildings and  bridges to take breathtaking photos and  post them on social media under the name  drifter shoots while the photos are  beautiful police in several cities  including cincinnati and new orleans say  wright committed crimes such as burglary  to take these photos wright said he's an  artist and the photography helps with  his post-traumatic stress disorder the  judge in a cincinnati case has ordered a  psychiatric evaluation to determine the  best way to proceed with the case  when we come back testimony in arizona  for the man charged with the murder of  27 year old sasha krauss the latest on  the mennonite murder trial when we come  back  [Music]  welcome back well just when we thought  we were done with robert durst there is  still more to uncover for the infamous  real estate heir his first wise family  announces they want to pursue charges  against his current wife  earlier this month durst was convicted  of murdering his best friend susan  berman t