nshot wound  injury of the head and a blunt force  injury of the  head dina rarely does a medical  examiner's testimony connect the murder  to the murderer but does the evidence  come from the fact that the bullet  came from this gun and can be traced  back to gucci's possession does that  create a more incentive that he should  be found guilty  yeah i mean there isn't any dna evidence  on pim so this ballistic evidence and  the connection that the examiner makes  that yes one of the causes of death was  from a bullet it was from a bullet that  he owned his brother has already been  charged with trying to retrieve it after  the announcement of her death is a very  strong piece of evidence for the  prosecution  no terry the medical examiner said that  the cause of death was a gunshot wound  to the head and blunt force trauma to  the head does that indicate anything to  you  it does brian the testimony of a medical  examiner is always critical and  especially if you have a murder case  like this he's saying it's blunt force  trauma to the head a gunshot wound to  the head to me that indicates this was  intentional and it was planned out it is  an execution style murder so when  there's something like that you have to  look at what the motive might have been  and here we already know from evidence  that we've talked about there were texts  about his disdain for the mennonite  religion and if that's the case as an  investigator what i would do is look for  all of that information tie it back to  the motive and that way they have a very  strong case  speaking of strong cases it seems like  something's missing in this case terry  we have as you said those text messages  for disdain for the mennonite community  you have a sunday school teacher not  just someone who is a part of religion  but participates pretty heavily in it  why do you think there are no hate crime  charges in this case  brian that's an excellent point and  maybe if we have some more evidence down  the li